{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CftGW9NQLuMdWUYtxiBGb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ay1s52SpdCU6WtKHARYfq7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/miryalasathvika/t2v-subjects/plain-agent/IS-seat-L2/Progetto-IS-main-English; grep -n \"reservations\\|fetch\\|api\" JavaProject/src/main/resources/static/app.js | head -12; grep -n \"reservations/\" JavaProject/src/main/resources/static/*.html | head\nmkdir -p task2view-out/IS-seat-L2; cd task2view-out/IS-seat-L2\ncat > view-1.puml <<'EOF'\n@startuml view-1\ntitle View 1 - Components involved in seat booking (structure & responsibilities)\nskinparam componentStyle rectangle\nskinparam packageStyle rectangle\n\npackage \"boundary (UI / entry points)\" {\n  [Swing wizard\\nDateAndRoomSelection > TimeSlotSelection >\\nAreaSelection > SeatSelection >\\nReservationSummary > ReservationConfirmed] as Swing\n  [StudentDashboard (Swing)\\ncancel / check-in / history] as Dash\n  [ReservationController\\n(REST /api/reservations:\\ncreate, cancel, checkIn)] as RC\n  [RestExceptionHandler\\nIllegalArgument/IllegalState -> HTTP error] as REH\n  [NotificationScheduler\\n@Scheduled every 60s] as Sched\n  [Static web app (app.js, reservation.html)] as Web\n}\n\npackage \"controller (use-case logic)\" {\n  [LibraryFacade\\nsingleton, pure delegation] as Facade\n  [ReservationManager\\nBOOKING RULES: makeReservation (UC7),\\ncancel (UC9), checkIn (UC10),\\nmanageReservationEnd (UC16)] as RM\n  [StudyRoomManager\\nrooms/slots/seat map for the wizard\\n(getAvailableTimeSlots, getRoomDetail)] as SRM\n  [NotificationManager\\nObserver of Reservation] as NM\n  interface AssignmentStrategy\n  [FirstAvailableAssignment] as FAA\n}\n\npackage \"entity (domain model)\" {\n  [Reservation\\n<<Subject>> state, date, cancel window (6h),\\ncheck-in tolerance (10 min)] as Res\n  [ReservationState\\nActive / Confirmed / Cancelled /\\nExpired / Completed] as St\n  [Student\\nhasActiveOrConfirmedReservationForDateAndSlot] as Stu\n  [StudyRoom\\nisOpenOnDate, getScheduledTimeSlots] as Room\n  [Area\\ngetAvailableSeats] as Area\n  [Seat\\nisAvailable] as Seat\n  [TimeSlot] as TS\n  [ReservationRegistry] as RR\n  [StudyRoomRegistry] as SRR\n  [UserRegistry] as UR\n}\n\npackage \"database\" {\n  [PersistenceManager (JPA)] as PM\n}\npackage \"boundary adapters\" {\n  [NotificationServiceAdapter /\\nExternalEmailGateway] as Mail\n}\ndatabase \"DB (persistence.xml)\" as DB\n\nSwing --> Facade\nDash --> Facade\nWeb --> RC : HTTP\nRC --> Facade\nRC ..> REH\nSched --> Facade\nFacade --> RM\nFacade --> SRM\nFacade --> NM\nRM --> RR\nRM --> SRR\nRM --> UR\nRM ..> AssignmentStrategy\nFAA ..|> AssignmentStrategy\nRM --> Res : create / cancel / checkIn\nRM --> Stu : uniqueness rule\nRM --> Area : available seats\nRes --> St\nRes ..> NM : notifyObservers (Observer)\nStu --> RR\nSeat --> RR : occupancy check\nArea --> Seat\nArea --> SRR\nRoom --> Area\nRes --> Seat\nRes --> TS\nSRM --> SRR\nSRM --> RR\nRR --> PM\nSRR --> PM\nUR --> PM\nPM --> DB\nNM --> Mail\n@enduml\nEOF\ncat > view-2.puml <<'EOF'\n@startuml view-2\ntitle View 2 - makeReservation (UC7) interaction: where each booking rule lives\nactor Student\nparticipant \"UI (Swing ReservationSummary /\\nReservationController)\" as UI\nparticipant LibraryFacade as F\nparticipant ReservationManager as RM\nparticipant StudyRoomRegistry as SRR\nparticipant StudyRoom as Room\nparticipant Student as Stu\nparticipant Area\nparticipant Seat\nparticipant ReservationRegistry as RR\nparticipant AssignmentStrategy as AS\nparticipant Reservation as Res\nparticipant NotificationManager as NM\n\nStudent -> UI : room, area, seat (0 = auto), date, slot\nUI -> F : makeReservation(ReservationRequestDTO)\nF -> RM : makeReservation(request)\nRM -> RM : resolveStudent (UserRegistry)\nRM -> SRR : resolveRoom: exists, active\nRM -> Room : isOpenOnDate (weekdays only)\nRM -> RM : resolveArea (area belongs to room)\nRM -> Room : resolveTimeSlot: getScheduledTimeSlots,\\nnot past / not already started\nRM -> RM : validateSeatInArea\nRM -> RM : synchronized(this)\ngroup RULE: one reservation per student/date/slot\n  RM -> Stu : hasActiveOrConfirmedReservationForDateAndSlot\n  Stu -> RR : findActiveReservations\nend\ngroup RULE: seat availability\n  RM -> Area : getAvailableSeats(date, slot)\n  Area -> Seat : isAvailable\n  Seat -> RR : findReservationsBySeat\nend\ngroup RULE: seat choice\n  alt seatId > 0\n    RM -> Seat : isAvailable (explicit seat)\n  else seatId == 0\n    RM -> AS : selectSeat(available) (FirstAvailable)\n  end\nend\nRM -> Res : new, setState(ActiveState)\nRM -> RR : saveReservation -> PersistenceManager\nRM -> Res : attach(NM); notifyObservers()\nRes -> NM : update -> email \"registered\"\nRM --> F : ReservationDTO\nF --> UI\nnote over UI\nErrors are IllegalArgument/IllegalStateException;\nREST maps them via RestExceptionHandler.\nend note\n@enduml\nEOF\ncat > view-3.puml <<'EOF'\n@startuml view-3\ntitle View 3 - Reservation lifecycle (State pattern) and rules tied to it\n[*] --> ACTIVE : makeReservation (UC7)\nACTIVE --> CANCELLED : cancel (UC9)\\nrule: owner only, >= 6h before slot start\nACTIVE --> CONFIRMED : check-in (UC10)\\nrule: same day, <= 10 min after start\nACTIVE --> EXPIRED : manageEnd (UC16, scheduler)\\nstart + 10 min passed, no check-in\nCONFIRMED --> COMPLETED : manageEnd (UC16)\\nslot end passed\nCANCELLED --> CANCELLED : forceCancel when room deleted\\n(StudyRoomManager.deleteStudyRoom)\nnote right of ACTIVE\nACTIVE and CONFIRMED occupy the seat\n(ReservationRegistry.occupiesSlot):\nused by Seat.isAvailable, uniqueness rule,\nroom monitoring and statistics.\nend note\nnote bottom\nEvery setState() notifies observers (NotificationManager -> email).\nConfirmedState cancel/checkIn return false.\nend note\n@enduml\nEOF\ncat > view-4.puml <<'EOF'\n@startuml view-4\ntitle View 4 - Impact map: what a change to booking rules can touch\nskinparam componentStyle rectangle\ncomponent \"ReservationManager\\n(primary change point:\\nvalidations in makeReservation)\" as RM #LightCoral\ncomponent \"Reservation\\n(cancel window, check-in tolerance,\\nCHECK_IN_TOLERANCE_MINUTES)\" as Res #LightCoral\ncomponent \"Student.hasActiveOrConfirmed...\\n(uniqueness rule)\" as Stu #LightCoral\ncomponent \"AssignmentStrategy /\\nFirstAvailableAssignment\\n(auto seat choice)\" as AS #LightCoral\ncomponent \"ReservationRequestDTO /\\nReservationDTO\\n(new rule inputs/outputs)\" as DTO #Gold\ncomponent \"ReservationController\\n(request params)\" as RC #Gold\ncomponent \"Swing wizard + app.js\\n(new inputs, error display)\" as UI #Gold\ncomponent \"RestExceptionHandler\" as REH #Gold\ncomponent \"Seat / Area / StudyRoom\\nisAvailable, getAvailableSeats,\\nisOpenOnDate\" as Avail #Gold\ncomponent \"ReservationRegistry.occupiesSlot\\n+ queries\" as RR #Gold\ncomponent \"StudyRoomManager\\n(getRoomDetail, getAvailableTimeSlots,\\nmonitoraSale, deleteStudyRoom)\" as SRM #Gold\ncomponent \"ReservationManager statistics\\n+ manageReservationEnd\" as Stat #Gold\ncomponent \"NotificationManager\\n(messages per state)\" as NM #LightGreen\ncomponent \"Reservation entity mapping\\n(persistence.xml schema)\" as DB #LightGreen\ncomponent \"Tests: MakeReservationTest,\\nCancelReservationTest, PerformCheckInTest,\\nManageReservationEndTest, AvailableStudyRoomsQueryTest\" as T #LightGreen\n\nRM --> Res\nRM --> Stu\nRM --> AS\nRM --> DTO\nRC --> DTO\nUI --> RC\nUI ..> DTO\nREH ..> RM : exception types\nRM ..> Avail\nAvail --> RR\nSRM --> RR : seat map shows availability\nStat --> RR\nRes --> NM\nRes --> DB : new fields need schema change\nT ..> RM\nlegend right\nRed = likely edited; Yellow = check for consistency;\nGreen = secondary (tests, messages, schema).\nend legend\n@enduml\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Seat booking - architecture views (IS-seat-L2)\n\nSource: JavaProject (Java, Spring Boot REST + Swing UI, JPA). Layers: boundary / controller / entity / database.\n\n- **view-1.puml** - Component view. Shows the components involved in seat booking, their responsibilities and dependencies (UI -> LibraryFacade -> ReservationManager -> entities/registries -> PersistenceManager; Observer to NotificationManager; AssignmentStrategy). Why: answers \"what are the main parts and how do they connect\".\n- **view-2.puml** - Sequence of `makeReservation` (UC7). Shows the order of checks and exactly where each existing booking rule is implemented (room open/active, slot not past, one reservation per student/date/slot, seat availability, explicit vs auto seat, save, notify). Why: this is where new rules will be inserted.\n- **view-3.puml** - Reservation state machine (State pattern). Shows statuses and the time-based rules (6h cancel window, 10 min check-in tolerance, expiry/completion by the scheduler). Why: new rules often interact with lifecycle and with which states \"occupy\" a seat.\n- **view-4.puml** - Impact map. Classifies elements as primary (red), to-verify (yellow), secondary (green) for a rule change. Why: addresses \"which parts may be affected\"; this is my analysis derived from the dependencies in the code, not code structure itself.\n\nNotes: Swing and REST both enter via `LibraryFacade` (Swing directly, REST through `ReservationController`). Rule constants are hard-coded (6h in `Reservation.validateCancellationWindow`, 10 min in `Reservation.CHECK_IN_TOLERANCE_MINUTES`). `ReservationManager.makeReservation` is `synchronized` to guard concurrent booking. Not rendered with PlantUML here; sources only.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3163,"cache_read_input_tokens":57443,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3163},"output_tokens":28,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8029d137-1b9c-4d38-af2e-2dc09b578b50","uuid":"755aa99e-5bf3-472d-ae4c-fc4e2a2edcef","timestamp":"2026-10-10T08:49:27.661Z","request_id":"req_011CftGW91aXtqtDSWwthgKC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Ay1s52SpdCU6WtKHARYfq7":{"command":"cd /Users/miryalasathvika/t2v-subjects/plain-agent/IS-seat-L2/Progetto-IS-main-English; grep -n \"reservations\\|fetch\\|api\" JavaProject/src/main/resources/static/app.js | head -12; grep -n \"reservations/\" JavaProject/src/main/resources/static/*.html | head\nmkdir -p task2view-out/IS-seat-L2; cd task2view-out/IS-seat-L2\ncat > view-1.puml <<'EOF'\n@startuml view-1\ntitle View 1 - Components involved in seat booking (structure & responsibilities)\nskinparam componentStyle rectangle\nskinparam packageStyle rectangle\n\npackage \"boundary (UI / entry points)\" {\n  [Swing wizard\\nDateAndRoomSelection > TimeSlotSelection >\\nAreaSelection > SeatSelection >\\nReservationSummary > ReservationConfirmed] as Swing\n  [StudentDashboard (Swing)\\ncancel / check-in / history] as Dash\n  [ReservationController\\n(REST /api/reservations:\\ncreate, cancel, checkIn)] as RC\n  [RestExceptionHandler\\nIllegalArgument/IllegalState -> HTTP error] as REH\n  [NotificationScheduler\\n@Scheduled every 60s] as Sched\n  [Static web app (app.js, reservation.html)] as Web\n}\n\npackage \"controller (use-case logic)\" {\n  [LibraryFacade\\nsingleton, pure delegation] as Facade\n  [ReservationManager\\nBOOKING RULES: makeReservation (UC7),\\ncancel (UC9), checkIn (UC10),\\nmanageReservationEnd (UC16)] as RM\n  [StudyRoomManager\\nrooms/slots/seat map for the wizard\\n(getAvailableTimeSlots, getRoomDetail)] as SRM\n  [NotificationManager\\nObserver of Reservation] as NM\n  interface AssignmentStrategy\n  [FirstAvailableAssignment] as FAA\n}\n\npackage \"entity (domain model)\" {\n  [Reservation\\n<<Subject>> state, date, cancel window (6h),\\ncheck-in tolerance (10 min)] as Res\n  [ReservationState\\nActive / Confirmed / Cancelled /\\nExpired / Completed] as St\n  [Student\\nhasActiveOrConfirmedReservationForDateAndSlot] as Stu\n  [StudyRoom\\nisOpenOnDate, getScheduledTimeSlots] as Room\n  [Area\\ngetAvailableSeats] as Area\n  [Seat\\nisAvailable] as Seat\n  [TimeSlot] as TS\n  [ReservationRegistry] as RR\n  [StudyRoomRegistry] as SRR\n  [UserRegistry] as UR\n}\n\npackage \"database\" {\n  [PersistenceManager (JPA)] as PM\n}\npackage \"boundary adapters\" {\n  [NotificationServiceAdapter /\\nExternalEmailGateway] as Mail\n}\ndatabase \"DB (persistence.xml)\" as DB\n\nSwing --> Facade\nDash --> Facade\nWeb --> RC : HTTP\nRC --> Facade\nRC ..> REH\nSched --> Facade\nFacade --> RM\nFacade --> SRM\nFacade --> NM\nRM --> RR\nRM --> SRR\nRM --> UR\nRM ..> AssignmentStrategy\nFAA ..|> AssignmentStrategy\nRM --> Res : create / cancel / checkIn\nRM --> Stu : uniqueness rule\nRM --> Area : available seats\nRes --> St\nRes ..> NM : notifyObservers (Observer)\nStu --> RR\nSeat --> RR : occupancy check\nArea --> Seat\nArea --> SRR\nRoom --> Area\nRes --> Seat\nRes --> TS\nSRM --> SRR\nSRM --> RR\nRR --> PM\nSRR --> PM\nUR --> PM\nPM --> DB\nNM --> Mail\n@enduml\nEOF\ncat > view-2.puml <<'EOF'\n@startuml view-2\ntitle View 2 - makeReservation (UC7) interaction: where each booking rule lives\nactor Student\nparticipant \"UI (Swing ReservationSummary /\\nReservationController)\" as UI\nparticipant LibraryFacade as F\nparticipant ReservationManager as RM\nparticipant StudyRoomRegistry as SRR\nparticipant StudyRoom as Room\nparticipant Student as Stu\nparticipant Area\nparticipant Seat\nparticipant ReservationRegistry as RR\nparticipant AssignmentStrategy as AS\nparticipant Reservation as Res\nparticipant NotificationManager as NM\n\nStudent -> UI : room, area, seat (0 = auto), date, slot\nUI -> F : makeReservation(ReservationRequestDTO)\nF -> RM : makeReservation(request)\nRM -> RM : resolveStudent (UserRegistry)\nRM -> SRR : resolveRoom: exists, active\nRM -> Room : isOpenOnDate (weekdays only)\nRM -> RM : resolveArea (area belongs to room)\nRM -> Room : resolveTimeSlot: getScheduledTimeSlots,\\nnot past / not already started\nRM -> RM : validateSeatInArea\nRM -> RM : synchronized(this)\ngroup RULE: one reservation per student/date/slot\n  RM -> Stu : hasActiveOrConfirmedReservationForDateAndSlot\n  Stu -> RR : findActiveReservations\nend\ngroup RULE: seat availability\n  RM -> Area : getAvailableSeats(date, slot)\n  Area -> Seat : isAvailable\n  Seat -> RR : findReservationsBySeat\nend\ngroup RULE: seat choice\n  alt seatId > 0\n    RM -> Seat : isAvailable (explicit seat)\n  else seatId == 0\n    RM -> AS : selectSeat(available) (FirstAvailable)\n  end\nend\nRM -> Res : new, setState(ActiveState)\nRM -> RR : saveReservation -> PersistenceManager\nRM -> Res : attach(NM); notifyObservers()\nRes -> NM : update -> email \"registered\"\nRM --> F : ReservationDTO\nF --> UI\nnote over UI\nErrors are IllegalArgument/IllegalStateException;\nREST maps them via RestExceptionHandler.\nend note\n@enduml\nEOF\ncat > view-3.puml <<'EOF'\n@startuml view-3\ntitle View 3 - Reservation lifecycle (State pattern) and rules tied to it\n[*] --> ACTIVE : makeReservation (UC7)\nACTIVE --> CANCELLED : cancel (UC9)\\nrule: owner only, >= 6h before slot start\nACTIVE --> CONFIRMED : check-in (UC10)\\nrule: same day, <= 10 min after start\nACTIVE --> EXPIRED : manageEnd (UC16, scheduler)\\nstart + 10 min passed, no check-in\nCONFIRMED --> COMPLETED : manageEnd (UC16)\\nslot end passed\nCANCELLED --> CANCELLED : forceCancel when room deleted\\n(StudyRoomManager.deleteStudyRoom)\nnote right of ACTIVE\nACTIVE and CONFIRMED occupy the seat\n(ReservationRegistry.occupiesSlot):\nused by Seat.isAvailable, uniqueness rule,\nroom monitoring and statistics.\nend note\nnote bottom\nEvery setState() notifies observers (NotificationManager -> email).\nConfirmedState cancel/checkIn return false.\nend note\n@enduml\nEOF\ncat > view-4.puml <<'EOF'\n@startuml view-4\ntitle View 4 - Impact map: what a change to booking rules can touch\nskinparam componentStyle rectangle\ncomponent \"ReservationManager\\n(primary change point:\\nvalidations in makeReservation)\" as RM #LightCoral\ncomponent \"Reservation\\n(cancel window, check-in tolerance,\\nCHECK_IN_TOLERANCE_MINUTES)\" as Res #LightCoral\ncomponent \"Student.hasActiveOrConfirmed...\\n(uniqueness rule)\" as Stu #LightCoral\ncomponent \"AssignmentStrategy /\\nFirstAvailableAssignment\\n(auto seat choice)\" as AS #LightCoral\ncomponent \"ReservationRequestDTO /\\nReservationDTO\\n(new rule inputs/outputs)\" as DTO #Gold\ncomponent \"ReservationController\\n(request params)\" as RC #Gold\ncomponent \"Swing wizard + app.js\\n(new inputs, error display)\" as UI #Gold\ncomponent \"RestExceptionHandler\" as REH #Gold\ncomponent \"Seat / Area / StudyRoom\\nisAvailable, getAvailableSeats,\\nisOpenOnDate\" as Avail #Gold\ncomponent \"ReservationRegistry.occupiesSlot\\n+ queries\" as RR #Gold\ncomponent \"StudyRoomManager\\n(getRoomDetail, getAvailableTimeSlots,\\nmonitoraSale, deleteStudyRoom)\" as SRM #Gold\ncomponent \"ReservationManager statistics\\n+ manageReservationEnd\" as Stat #Gold\ncomponent \"NotificationManager\\n(messages per state)\" as NM #LightGreen\ncomponent \"Reservation entity mapping\\n(persistence.xml schema)\" as DB #LightGreen\ncomponent \"Tests: MakeReservationTest,\\nCancelReservationTest, PerformCheckInTest,\\nManageReservationEndTest, AvailableStudyRoomsQueryTest\" as T #LightGreen\n\nRM --> Res\nRM --> Stu\nRM --> AS\nRM --> DTO\nRC --> DTO\nUI --> RC\nUI ..> DTO\nREH ..> RM : exception types\nRM ..> Avail\nAvail --> RR\nSRM --> RR : seat map shows availability\nStat --> RR\nRes --> NM\nRes --> DB : new fields need schema change\nT ..> RM\nlegend right\nRed = likely edited; Yellow = check for consistency;\nGreen = secondary (tests, messages, schema).\nend legend\n@enduml\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Seat booking - architecture views (IS-seat-L2)\n\nSource: JavaProject (Java, Spring Boot REST + Swing UI, JPA). Layers: boundary / controller / entity / database.\n\n- **view-1.puml** - Component view. Shows the components involved in seat booking, their responsibilities and dependencies (UI -> LibraryFacade -> ReservationManager -> entities/registries -> PersistenceManager; Observer to NotificationManager; AssignmentStrategy). Why: answers \"what are the main parts and how do they connect\".\n- **view-2.puml** - Sequence of `makeReservation` (UC7). Shows the order of checks and exactly where each existing booking rule is implemented (room open/active, slot not past, one reservation per student/date/slot, seat availability, explicit vs auto seat, save, notify). Why: this is where new rules will be inserted.\n- **view-3.puml** - Reservation state machine (State pattern). Shows statuses and the time-based rules (6h cancel window, 10 min check-in tolerance, expiry/completion by the scheduler). Why: new rules often interact with lifecycle and with which states \"occupy\" a seat.\n- **view-4.puml** - Impact map. Classifies elements as primary (red), to-verify (yellow), secondary (green) for a rule change. Why: addresses \"which parts may be affected\"; this is my analysis derived from the dependencies in the code, not code structure itself.\n\nNotes: Swing and REST both enter via `LibraryFacade` (Swing directly, REST through `ReservationController`). Rule constants are hard-coded (6h in `Reservation.validateCancellationWindow`, 10 min in `Reservation.CHECK_IN_TOLERANCE_MINUTES`). `ReservationManager.makeReservation` is `synchronized` to guard concurrent booking. Not rendered with PlantUML here; sources only.\nEOF"}}}
